7</td></tr><tr><td colspan="5" align="left" rowspan="1">Thyroid hormones</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;T<sub>4</sub> [mean (&#x003bc;g/dL)]</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">7.5<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn12-ehp0115-001197">*</xref></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">7.3&#x02013;7.7</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">8.2<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn12-ehp0115-001197">*</xref></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">8.0&#x02013;8.5</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;T<sub>4</sub> [&#x0003c; 5.4 &#x003bc;g/dL (%)]</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">8.0<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn12-ehp0115-001197">*</xref></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5.3&#x02013;10.6</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3.2<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn12-ehp0115-001197">*</xref></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.5&#x02013;5.0</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;T<sub>4</sub> [&#x0003e; 12.8 &#x003bc;g/dL (%)]</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.1<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn12-ehp0115-001197">*</xref></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.0&#x02013;0.2</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.5<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn12-ehp0115-001197">*</xref></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.7&#x02013;2.3</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;TSH [geometric mean (IU/L)]</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.44</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.39&#x02013;1.50</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.46</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.39&#x02013;1.53</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;TSH [&#x0003c; 0.47 IU/L (%)]</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.9</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.5&#x02013;4.2</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3.8</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.7&#x02013;5.0</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;TSH [&#x0003e; 5.0 IU/L (%)]</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.4</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.4&#x02013;3.5</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.3</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.4&#x02013;3.2</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn8-ehp0115-001197"><p>NA, not applicable. Data were missing for cotinine (<italic>n</italic> = 21), BMI (<italic>n</italic> = 4), TSH (<italic>n</italic> = 3), pregnancy (<italic>n</italic> = 10), and completion of menopause (<italic>n</italic> = 25).</p></fn><fn id="tfn9-ehp0115-001197"><label>a</label><p>A total of 36 men and 114 women with thyroid disease (reported current thyroid disease or taking thyroid medications) were excluded from the analysis.</p></fn><fn id="tfn10-ehp0115-001197"><label>b</label><p>All estimates were adjusted for survey design and sample weights.</p></fn><fn id="tfn11-ehp0115-001197"><label>c</label><p>Includes amidoarone, carbamazepine, chlorpropamide, carbidopa/levodopa, heparin, interferon, lithium, phenytoin, phenobarbital, or sulfasalazine.</p></fn><fn id="tfn12-ehp0115-001197"><label>*</label><p>Significantly different by sex, <italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.05.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t4-ehp0115-001197" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p>Associations [&#x003b2; (95% CI)] of &#x02211;TEQs and &#x02211;PCBs with thyroid hormones in women without thyroid disease.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th colspan="3" align="center" rowspan="1">Association of total T<sub>4</sub> with<hr/></th><th colspan="3" align="center" rowspan="1">Association of Ln TSH with<hr/></th></tr><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Subgroup, cycle</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" c